cartridge "ANGLER 64/TONY BRANTNER/1992"
' ANGLER 64 - Tony Brantner, RUN magazine's ReRUN disk, July/August 1992
' (Commodore 64, machine language). ColecoVision port in Amy.
'
' The game: steer the tip of your fishing line in front of a fish. Once it
' bites it swims back and forth, slowly rising; hold the button to reel it
' in quickly. A hungry lunker swims near the top: a hooked fish that
' touches him is eaten. Fish weigh 4 to 7 pounds and are worth 10 points x
' the level. Catch 99 pounds before the timer runs out (100 at level 1,
' 3 less each level, one unit every 90 frames); each unit left is worth 100
' points. Missing the limit ends the game.
'
' Rules and numbers come from the original's machine code (orig/ANGLER_ML,
' disassembly c64/ml.s), one routine at a time; the names in brackets below
' are the C64 addresses. All positions are kept in C64 sprite coordinates
' (the logic is the original's, pixel for pixel); only the drawing maps
' them to the ColecoVision screen (FxOf, GyOf).
'
' Pace: the original's main loop ($0940) runs as fast as the C64 can; real
' VICE (x64sc, NTSC) measured 23.5 passes a frame with a free line and 22.4
' with a fish on the line (c64/vcap.py, vcap2.py). The port runs the same
' pass, 47 per two frames free and 45 per two frames hooked.
'
' Controls: either controller. Stick: move the line. Button: reel in.

const TSky = 128
const TWat = 129
const TSc2 = 130
const TSc3 = 131
const TSc4 = 132
